5. Troubleshooting

The main difference from the instructor's reference setup was the host platform.

The original instructions use VirtualBox on Windows, while my system uses an Apple M2 Mac. Due to the Apple Silicon architecture, I used UTM with Kali Linux ARM64 instead.

The existing Kali installation was retained to avoid affecting university-related files and configurations.

6. Snapshot and Recovery

After configuring the laboratory, a recovery point/snapshot was maintained for the Kali environment.

This provides a way to return to a known working state before performing future cybersecurity exercises that may modify the VM.

