7. Learning Outcomes

Through this Week 1 task, I gained practical experience with:

Setting up a virtual cybersecurity environment.
Running Kali Linux on Apple Silicon.
Configuring IPv4 networking and routing.
Testing Internet and DNS connectivity.
Verifying penetration-testing tools.
Using VM recovery mechanisms.
Troubleshooting virtualization and networking differences between platforms.
8. Security & Ethical Use

The laboratory is intended strictly for educational and authorized security testing. Any scanning, reconnaissance, or penetration-testing activities should only target systems that are owned by the tester or where explicit permission has been provided.

9. Conclusion

The Week 1 cybersecurity laboratory was successfully prepared using UTM on an Apple M2 Mac with Kali Linux ARM64. The required network configuration, connectivity, tool verification, file-sharing capabilities, and recovery considerations were addressed, providing a foundation for the upcoming cybersecurity tasks.
